        <h2>The questions worth asking.</h2>
        <div>
          <details open><summary>Is this another autonomous review bot?</summary><p>No. Rennet does the structural reading. You inspect, question, edit, and post the review another person sees.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does dual review mean the models decide by majority?</summary><p>No. Claude and Codex run independently. Agreement is evidence; disagreement is a signal for you, and Rennet never averages it away.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Does “local-first” mean nothing leaves my machine?</summary><p>Rennet itself sends nothing anywhere. The coding agent you use still talks to its provider under its own terms and sign-in, exactly as it does today.</p></details>
